## 17. Important Development Rules

1. Inspect the existing project before changing files.
2. Preserve existing working functionality.
3. Do not delete existing database records.
4. Reuse existing authentication where possible.
5. Do not create duplicate routes or database tables.
6. Use database migrations for schema changes.
7. Validate all backend requests.
8. Secure every admin route.
9. Implement authorization policies.
10. Use reusable UI components.
11. Optimize for mobile devices.
12. Test every important feature.
13. Do not use fake users or fake testimonials.
14. Keep the design consistent across all pages.
15. Ensure the website is production-ready.

